  "notes": "South has a potential loser in spades and at least 1 loser in diamonds. If clubs break 3-3, 3 discards will be available for South's low diamonds.\n\nSouth can play to virtually ensure the contract when spades are no worse than 3-1 and clubs are no worse than 4-2. South should begin by ruffing the opening heart lead with a middle trump, preserving the ♠2.\n\nA top spade honour is cashed. When both defenders follow low, South cashes the top clubs in his hand. A middle spade is next led out of the South hand, surrendering a trick to the ♠Q. If the ♠Q is taken, South will have created a dummy entry in trump. South will be able to get to the dummy and in the process draw the last trump (if any). Dummy's 3 clubs will provide 3 discards for South's 3 diamond losers.\n\nIf a defender holding 3 spades to the ♠Q ducks the second round of trump, South should draw the last trump and hope diamonds break 3-2.",
